@@ -101,6 +101,24 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can push the notifications that land in someone's tray to their phone and desktop.
+Push notifications are signed with a [VAPID](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8292) key pair, which you generate once and then keep:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails push:vapid_keys
+```
+
+Set the two values it prints in the `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` environment variables:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+People can then turn notifications on for each device they use from their notification settings.
+Without these variables, Fizzy simply doesn't offer push notifications.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
